course: dictionary
lesson: 7921
title: Reach: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Reach is a word with several meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. «The train reached the city.» Here reach means got to a place, so the train arrived there.
explain: «Keep medicines out of reach of children.» Out of reach means too far away to touch, so the medicine is kept where a small child cannot get it. Reach can also be a noun: your reach is how far you can stretch your arm.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a simpler word. In «reach 100 points», try "get to 100 points": it still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning. Always test your guess in the sentence.
fact: Reach can be a verb (to reach, reaches, reached, reaching) or a noun (a reach).
fact: To reach a place means to get to it, as in «A message is cut into many small packets, each labelled with the address it must reach.»
fact: To reach for something means to stretch your arm out to touch or take it.
fact: «Reach for the stars» is a figure of speech: it means aim high and try for big goals.
fact: Your reach is how far you can stretch, and «out of reach» means too far to touch.
exercise: «A message is cut into many small packets, each labelled with the address it must reach.» What does reach mean here? | *To arrive at the address | To break into pieces | To shout loudly at the address | To stretch your arm to touch it
exercise: «Keep medicines out of reach of children.» What does out of reach mean? | Lost forever | Very close to the table | *Too far away to touch | Hidden inside a box
exercise: «Light from the Sun takes about 8 minutes to reach Earth.» What does reach mean here? | Turn into heat | Shine very brightly | Stretch out to touch | *Get to, arrive at
test: «Thunderstorm clouds reach so high that their tops are far below freezing, even in summer.» What does reach mean here? | Break apart | *Extend up to a great height | Stretch your arm to touch | Run very fast
test: Which sentence uses reach to mean stretch your arm to touch something? | The bus will reach town at noon | *Please reach the biscuits down for me | Phone me, so I can reach you | We reached our goal of 100 points
exam: Which meaning fits «reach for the stars»? | *To aim high and try for big goals | To be late for school | To sleep for a long time | To pull a plate off the table
